hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1326","Yusuf bin Musa told us, and Ahmad bin Uthman bin Hakim Al-Awdi, he said: Al-Hasan bin Bishr told us, Yusuf said: Ibn Al-Musayyab Al-Bajli, And they said: He said: Al-Hakam bin Abdul-Malik told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Jaad, on the authority of his father, he said: Abdullah met a man, He said: Peace be upon you, Ibn Masoud. Abdullah said: God and His Messenger have spoken the truth. I heard the Messenger of God, peace be upon him, saying: “Indeed, among the signs of “The hour is for a man to pass through a mosque without praying two rak’ahs there, and for a man to not greet anyone except to whom he knows, and for a young man to honor an old man.” Ahmed bin Uthman said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said"
